<%# Opens the player's connections while the page is still parsing. See
    PlayerHelper#player_preconnect_origins for what each one is worth.

    dns-prefetch alongside preconnect is the usual pair: the name lookup alone is the part
    every browser will act on, and it is what is left if preconnect is ignored or the
    connection is dropped before the frame uses it.

    No `crossorigin`: an iframe navigation is a credentialed load, and browsers pool those
    separately from anonymous ones -- warming the wrong pool would buy nothing. %>
<% content_for :head do %>
  <% player_preconnect_origins(url, source).each do |origin| %>
    <link rel="dns-prefetch" href="<%= origin %>">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="<%= origin %>">
  <% end %>
<% end %>
